From bc2de87d3d3de6ad161f5347f8d37941591205ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZetOmega <70434161+ZetOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:33:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] signal: turn @Name in group replies into real mentions
 (extra.real_mentions)

Turn "@Name" in outgoing group messages into real Signal mentions.

platforms.signal.extra.real_mentions: true enables it. Names resolve via
platforms.signal.extra.mention_aliases ({name: number-or-uuid}), then via the
group's members matched against contact-book names and the profile names of
people seen in chat. Ambiguous names are skipped unless the person being
replied to disambiguates; non-members and the bot itself are never mentioned;
code spans/blocks and e-mail addresses are left alone. Offsets are computed in
UTF-16 units. If signal-cli rejects a mention, the message is resent as plain
"@Name" text.

Env fallback: SIGNAL_REAL_MENTIONS.
---
 gateway/platforms/signal.py                | 127 ++++++++++++
 tests/gateway/test_signal_real_mentions.py | 224 +++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 351 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/gateway/test_signal_real_mentions.py

